{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WyJ1Hnt45kre99rGmnWF3w","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: test-rel01.3\n     2→title: \"Test Suite: rel01.3 — du specification and differential test\"\n     3→release: rel01.3\n     4→\n     5→traces:\n     6→  - rel01.3-uc001-du\n     7→  - prd009-du R1\n     8→  - prd009-du R2\n     9→  - prd009-du R3\n    10→  - prd009-du R4\n    11→  - prd009-du R5\n    12→\n    13→preconditions:\n    14→  - Binaries exist under ./bin/ (built via mage build).\n    15→  - Reference binaries are installed via Homebrew gdu (coreutils).\n    16→  - Tests are run via go test ./cmd/du/... which invokes RunDiffTests from pkg/testutils.\n    17→  - All tests use LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent divergence.\n    18→  - No normalization is applied; du output is deterministic when both binaries run on the same directory on the same filesystem.\n    19→  - All block-count tests use -k to pin output to 1024-byte blocks and eliminate platform default divergence.\n    20→  - Tests use a fixture directory (testdata/du-fixture/) containing nested files of known sizes, a second subdirectory for multi-argument tests, and files of varied sizes.\n    21→  - Hard-link pairs are created in test setup (not committed) to test dedup. All files in the fixture are on the same filesystem as the test runner.\n    22→\n    23→test_cases:\n    24→  - name: du_default_recursive\n    25→    description: Default flags with -k on fixture directory; one line per subdirectory and root.\n    26→    inputs:\n    27→      args: [\"-k\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n    28→      stdin: null\n    29→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    30→    normalization: none\n    31→    expected:\n    32→      exit_code: 0\n    33→      stdout_structure: one \"SIZE\\tPATH\" line per subdirectory, ending with the root directory total\n    34→      stderr: \"\"\n    35→    traces:\n    36→      - prd009-du R1.1\n    37→      - prd009-du R1.2\n    38→      - prd009-du R1.3\n    39→\n    40→  - name: du_summary_mode\n    41→    description: -s prints only the total for each argument.\n    42→    inputs:\n    43→      args: [\"-sk\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n    44→      stdin: null\n    45→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    46→    normalization: none\n    47→    expected:\n    48→      exit_code: 0\n    49→      stdout_structure: one line with total size and path\n    50→      stderr: \"\"\n    51→    traces:\n    52→      - prd009-du R2.2\n    53→\n    54→  - name: du_all_files\n    55→    description: -a prints size for every file, not just directories.\n    56→    inputs:\n    57→      args: [\"-ak\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n    58→      stdin: null\n    59→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    60→    normalization: none\n    61→    expected:\n    62→      exit_code: 0\n    63→      stdout_structure: one line per file and directory in the tree\n    64→      stderr: \"\"\n    65→    traces:\n    66→      - prd009-du R2.3\n    67→\n    68→  - name: du_human_readable\n    69→    description: -h displays sizes as human-readable strings (K/M/G).\n    70→    inputs:\n    71→      args: [\"-h\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n    72→      stdin: null\n    73→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    74→    normalization: none\n    75→    expected:\n    76→      exit_code: 0\n    77→      stdout_structure: size values contain unit suffixes (K, M, G)\n    78→      stderr: \"\"\n    79→    traces:\n    80→      - prd009-du R2.1\n    81→\n    82→  - name: du_max_depth_1\n    83→    description: -d 1 limits output to the argument and its immediate children.\n    84→    inputs:\n    85→      args: [\"-k\", \"-d\", \"1\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n    86→      stdin: null\n    87→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    88→    normalization: none\n    89→    expected:\n    90→      exit_code: 0\n    91→      stdout_structure: lines for immediate subdirectories and the root; no deeper entries\n    92→      stderr: \"\"\n    93→    traces:\n    94→      - prd009-du R2.4\n    95→\n    96→  - name: du_grand_total\n    97→    description: -c prints a grand total \"total\" line after all arguments.\n    98→    inputs:\n    99→      args: [\"-ck\", \"testdata/du-fixture/subdir1\", \"testdata/du-fixture/subdir2\"]\n   100→      stdin: null\n   101→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   102→    normalization: none\n   103→    expected:\n   104→      exit_code: 0\n   105→      stdout_structure: per-argument lines followed by a \"SIZE\\ttotal\" line\n   106→      stderr: \"\"\n   107→    traces:\n   108→      - prd009-du R2.7\n   109→\n   110→  - name: du_hard_link_dedup\n   111→    description: 'A file hard-linked into two directories is counted only once. Setup: create testdata/du-hardlink-fixture/ with dir_a/shared.txt (a regular file) and dir_b/shared.txt (hard link to dir_a/shared.txt, same inode). The hard link is created at test time via os.Link.'\n   112→    inputs:\n   113→      args: [\"-k\", \"testdata/du-hardlink-fixture/\"]\n   114→      stdin: null\n   115→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   116→    normalization: none\n   117→    expected:\n   118→      exit_code: 0\n   119→      stdout_structure: total for the root counts shared.txt blocks once, not twice\n   120→      stderr: \"\"\n   121→    traces:\n   122→      - prd009-du R3.1\n   123→      - prd009-du R3.2\n   124→      - prd009-du R3.3\n   125→\n   126→  - name: du_apparent_size\n   127→    description: --apparent-size reports st_size instead of st_blocks.\n   128→    inputs:\n   129→      args: [\"--apparent-size\", \"-k\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n   130→      stdin: null\n   131→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   132→    normalization: none\n   133→    expected:\n   134→      exit_code: 0\n   135→      stdout_structure: sizes based on file content length, not block allocation\n   136→      stderr: \"\"\n   137→    traces:\n   138→      - prd009-du R2.8\n   139→\n   140→  - name: du_kilobyte_units\n   141→    description: -k reports in 1024-byte blocks (default, accepted without error).\n   142→    inputs:\n   143→      args: [\"-k\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n   144→      stdin: null\n   145→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   146→    normalization: none\n   147→    expected:\n   148→      exit_code: 0\n   149→      stdout_structure: identical to default_recursive (1K is the default)\n   150→      stderr: \"\"\n   151→    traces:\n   152→      - prd009-du R2.5\n   153→\n   154→  - name: du_megabyte_units\n   155→    description: -m reports in 1048576-byte (1M) blocks.\n   156→    inputs:\n   157→      args: [\"-m\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n   158→      stdin: null\n   159→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   160→    normalization: none\n   161→    expected:\n   162→      exit_code: 0\n   163→      stdout_structure: sizes in megabyte units, smaller values show as 1 (rounded up)\n   164→      stderr: \"\"\n   165→    traces:\n   166→      - prd009-du R2.6\n   167→\n   168→  - name: du_missing_path\n   169→    description: Non-existent argument prints error to stderr, exits 1.\n   170→    inputs:\n   171→      args: [\"-k\", \"nonexistent_dir\"]\n   172→      stdin: null\n   173→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   174→    normalization: none\n   175→    expected:\n   176→      exit_code: 0\n   177→      stderr_contains: \"nonexistent_dir\"\n   178→    traces:\n   179→      - prd009-du R4.2\n   180→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01TYkzfVfiafWLqmfhdyEAb4","session_id":"ffcf16cc-f1bd-4af0-8cf7-4be580f5f5ef","uuid":"8b06d0d9-613b-4755-8810-3d843e71ee22"}
